---
import ArchwayLayout from '../layouts/ArchwayLayout.astro';
import HeroGatedReveal from '../components/shared/HeroGatedReveal.astro';
import ProblemCardsThree from '../components/shared/ProblemCardsThree.astro';
import StatsBar from '../components/shared/StatsBar.astro';
import AboutArchway from '../components/shared/AboutArchway.astro';
import WhyChooseUs from '../components/shared/WhyChooseUs.astro';
import Testimonials from '../components/shared/Testimonials.astro';
import BottomCTA from '../components/shared/BottomCTA.astro';

const FORM_ID = 'a25f33ac-dd5d-4af5-a861-25805cbfdb9d'; // TODO: swap for this page's own HubSpot form ID before launch
---

<ArchwayLayout
  title="Free Pen Test Readiness Checklist for Independent Insurance Agencies | Archway"
  description="Run the free pen test readiness checklist for agency owners. 17 items, self-scored, to see where your agency stands before your next cyber liability renewal."
  ctaText="Get the Free Checklist"
  ctaHref="#hero-form"
>
  <HeroGatedReveal
    badge="For Independent Insurance Agencies"
    headline="Your carrier will ask if you have been tested. <span class='hl'>Could you prove&nbsp;it?</span>"
    subhead="A 17-item self-audit for agency owners. Check what is true for your agency and see where you stand. No IT background required."
    formHeading="Get the Free Checklist"
    formSubhead="Fill this out and your checklist appears right here on the page."
    formId={FORM_ID}
    trustLine="Written for independent insurance agencies running Applied Epic, AMS360, HawkSoft, or EZLynx. We work with one kind of business, and only that."
    revealHeading="Your checklist is unlocked"
  >
    <h2 class="g-title">Your Pen Test Readiness Checklist</h2>
    <p class="g-lead">Seventeen items across four areas. Check what is true for your agency, count what you cannot confirm, and you will know whether you could answer the renewal question with documentation today.</p>
    <p class="g-note">This is the read-only checklist. Interactive scoring that posts your result to Archway is coming in Q3.</p>

    <p class="g-area">1. Do You Need a Test — And Could You Prove It?</p>
    <div class="g-checklist">
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>Your last cyber liability application asked whether you were penetration tested in the last 12 months</h4><p>If the question is on the form, your answer is on the record. Knowing it was asked is the first step to answering it honestly.</p></div></div>
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>You can explain the difference between a vulnerability scan and a penetration test</h4><p>A scan flags known weaknesses automatically. A test is a person trying to break in. Carriers mean the second one, and the two are not interchangeable on an application.</p></div></div>
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>You know whether NYDFS or an equivalent state regulation applies to your agency</h4><p>If you write in a regulated state, testing may not be optional. Knowing your exposure tells you whether this is a nice-to-have or a requirement.</p></div></div>
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>A "yes" to the testing question would be defensible if a carrier asked for proof today</h4><p>Answering yes is easy. Backing it up with a dated report is what actually matters when a claim or audit lands.</p></div></div>
    </div>

    <p class="g-area">2. The Controls a Pen Test Checks</p>
    <div class="g-checklist">
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>MFA is enforced on every account, not just enabled and available</h4><p>An optional MFA setting that staff can skip is the same as no MFA to a tester. Enforcement is what closes the door.</p></div></div>
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>Your backups have been tested by actually restoring from them</h4><p>A backup you have never restored is a guess. A test proves it works before ransomware forces the question.</p></div></div>
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>You have a written incident response plan reviewed in the last 12 months</h4><p>When something goes wrong, you do not want to be writing the plan at the same time. A current, written plan is what carriers expect to see.</p></div></div>
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>Endpoint detection and response is installed on every workstation and server</h4><p>One unprotected machine is the way in. Coverage everywhere, not just on the owner's laptop, is what a test looks for.</p></div></div>
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>Accounts are removed promptly when someone leaves the agency</h4><p>A former producer's still-active login is an open door nobody is watching. Prompt removal is a control a tester will probe.</p></div></div>
    </div>

    <p class="g-area">3. Proof You Can Produce</p>
    <div class="g-checklist">
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>You can produce a current pen test report within 24 hours of a carrier request</h4><p>Having been tested is not the same as being able to prove it fast. Carriers and claims adjusters work on deadlines.</p></div></div>
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>Your security controls are documented in writing, not just described from memory</h4><p>"We have MFA" is a description. A written policy with screenshots is evidence. Only one of them holds up under scrutiny.</p></div></div>
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>The answers on your cyber application match what is actually in place today</h4><p>An application that overstates your controls is a problem waiting for a claim. The form and the reality need to agree.</p></div></div>
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>You know where your security documentation lives and can find it without asking IT</h4><p>Documentation you cannot locate is documentation you do not have when it counts. The owner should be able to put hands on it.</p></div></div>
    </div>

    <p class="g-area">4. Your Environment</p>
    <div class="g-checklist">
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>You know whether your AMS is cloud-hosted or running on a local server</h4><p>Where your management system lives changes what a test needs to cover. A local server in the back office is a different risk profile than a hosted platform.</p></div></div>
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>You know what parts of your network are exposed to the internet</h4><p>Anything reachable from outside is something an attacker can reach too. Knowing what is exposed is the start of defending it.</p></div></div>
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>You know exactly who holds administrator access across your systems</h4><p>Admin access is the keys to the building. If the list surprises you, that is itself a finding a test would flag.</p></div></div>
      <div class="g-check-item"><span class="g-check-box"></span><div><h4>It has been less than 12 months since your last security assessment</h4><p>Environments drift. A test from two years ago does not describe the network you run today, and carriers know it.</p></div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="g-cta">
      <h3>Want a real test scoped for your agency?</h3>
      <p>Run the checklist, then request a scoping call. We will scope a pen test to your agency size — no calendar games, a real conversation.</p>
      <a class="g-cta-btn" href="/book-compliance-review">Request a scoping call</a>
    </div>
  </HeroGatedReveal>

  <section class="context-section">
    <div class="context-inner fade-up">
      <div class="context-aside">
        <span class="context-eyebrow">Why this matters</span>
        <h2 class="context-lead">A lot of agencies answer yes when the honest answer is&nbsp;no.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="context-body">
        <p>More cyber liability applications ask the same question every year: <strong>has your network been penetration tested in the last 12 months?</strong> Agencies confuse the term with vulnerability scans and general security, so the answer that goes on the application is not always the honest one.</p>
        <p>This checklist clears it up. Seventeen items across four areas, each with a one-line reason it matters. Check Yes, No, or Not sure for your agency, count your gaps, and see whether you could answer that renewal question with documentation today.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ProblemCardsThree
    sectionLabel="What the Checklist Covers"
    heading="Four Areas. <br /><span class='hl'>Seventeen Honest&nbsp;Questions.</span>"
    subhead="Each item has a one-line reason it matters. Check what is true for your agency and count the gaps."
    cards={[
      {
        title: "Do you need a test, and could you prove it?",
        body: "NYDFS or equivalent exposure, what your cyber application asks, scan vs test, and whether a yes would be defensible today."
      },
      {
        title: "The controls a test checks",
        body: "MFA enforced not just enabled, tested backups, a current incident response plan, endpoint detection everywhere, and prompt account removal."
      },
      {
        title: "Proof you can produce",
        body: "A current test report, written evidence rather than description, application answers that match reality, and documentation you can actually find."
      },
      {
        title: "Your environment",
        body: "Whether your AMS is cloud-hosted or on a local server, what is exposed to the internet, who holds admin access, and time since your last assessment."
      }
    ]}
  />

  <StatsBar />
  <AboutArchway />
  <WhyChooseUs />
  <Testimonials />

  <BottomCTA
    heading="Want to Know Where You Stand Before Renewal?"
    subtext="Run the checklist, then book a scoping call if you want a real test scoped for your agency size."
    ctaText="Get the Free Checklist"
    ctaHref="#hero-form"
  />
</ArchwayLayout>

<style>
  :global(.problem-header h2 .hl) { color: var(--orange); }
  .context-section { background: var(--light-bg); padding: 72px 24px; }
  .context-inner { max-width: 1040px; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.82fr 1.18fr; gap: 56px; align-items: start; }
  .context-aside { border-left: 3px solid var(--orange); padding-left: 24px; }
  .context-eyebrow { display: block; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--orange); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .context-lead { font-size: 27px; font-weight: 800; color: var(--charcoal); line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -0.5px; margin: 0; }
  .context-body p { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-light); margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .context-body p strong { color: var(--charcoal); font-weight: 700; }
  .context-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .context-inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
    .context-aside { border-left: none; padding-left: 0; border-top: 3px solid var(--orange); padding-top: 20px; }
    .context-lead { font-size: 23px; }
  }
  .g-title { font-size: 30px; font-weight: 800; color: var(--charcoal); line-height: 1.25; margin-bottom: 16px; letter-spacing: -0.5px; }
  .g-lead { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-light); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .g-note { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-light); font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .g-area { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--orange); margin: 28px 0 12px; }
  .g-checklist { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .g-check-item { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 22px 1fr; gap: 14px; align-items: flex-start; padding: 16px 20px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid var(--card-border); border-radius: 10px; }
  .g-check-box { width: 22px; height: 22px; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 6px; margin-top: 2px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .g-check-item h4 { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--charcoal); margin: 0 0 3px; line-height: 1.4; }
  .g-check-item p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-light); margin: 0; }
  .g-cta { background: var(--navy); border-radius: 14px; padding: 32px 36px; margin-top: 36px; }
  .g-cta h3 { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 800; color: #ffffff; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.3; }
  .g-cta p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8); margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .g-cta-btn { display: inline-block; background: var(--orange); color: #ffffff; padding: 14px 28px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 700; transition: background 0.2s; }
  .g-cta-btn:hover { background: var(--orange-dark); }
  @media (max-width: 768px) { .g-title { font-size: 25px; } }
</style>
